        "transition": {
          "type": "smooth",
          "time": 1
        },
        "layerOverride": [],
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "## Mumbai, India\n\nGlobal warming is not a local heat index. India is included alongside African contexts. All facility values are fictional; this point is a city anchor and has no real facility funding status.\n\n**Synthetic teaching scenario.** Not observations, forecasts or PEPFAR facility locations.\n\nExplore the [scenario dashboard](https://jltobias.github.io/JupyterLite-Climate-and-Health/explore/?case=mumbai)."
        }
      }
    },
    "beira-story": {
      "name": "Beira: climate and health",
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 5,
        "extent": [
          2876495.64209819,
          -3354026.586003257,
          4880246.476377114,
          -1212833.8167833053
        ],
        "transition": {
          "type": "smooth",
          "time": 1
        },
        "layerOverride": [],
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "## Beira, Mozambique\n\nA dry building may be isolated by an access route. Compare an invented road elevation with a water plane; no tide, surge, drainage or hydrologic connectivity is modeled.\n\n**Synthetic teaching scenario.** Not observations, forecasts or PEPFAR facility locations.\n\nExplore the [scenario dashboard](https://jltobias.github.io/JupyterLite-Climate-and-Health/explore/?case=beira)."
        }
      }
    },
    "mombasa-story": {
      "name": "Mombasa: climate and health",
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 5,
        "extent": [
          3414168.7826297004,
          -1464302.5465990214,
          5417919.616908625,
          552835.6048836526
        ],
        "transition": {
          "type": "smooth",
          "time": 1
        },
        "layerOverride": [],
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "## Mombasa, Kenya\n\nEvaluate appropriate shade, water harvesting, reliable power and access engineering. Mangroves, seagrass and reef health have local ecological context; no universal flood-protection factor is assumed.\n\n**Synthetic teaching scenario.** Not observations, forecasts or PEPFAR facility locations.\n\nExplore the [scenario dashboard](https://jltobias.github.io/JupyterLite-Climate-and-Health/explore/?case=mombasa)."
        }
      }
    },
    "lusaka-story": {
      "name": "Lusaka: climate and health",
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 5,
        "extent": [
          2146239.782494315,
          -2801003.832602355,
          4149990.616773239,
          -712810.7584889357
        ],
        "transition": {
          "type": "smooth",
          "time": 1
        },
        "layerOverride": [],
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "## Lusaka, Zambia\n\nThis inland case has no marine exposure in the toy model. Identify water and electricity bottlenecks and discuss medicine supply, staffing and referrals for HIV/TB continuity.\n\n**Synthetic teaching scenario.** Not observations, forecasts or PEPFAR facility locations.\n\nExplore the [scenario dashboard](https://jltobias.github.io/JupyterLite-Climate-and-Health/explore/?case=lusaka)."
        }
      }
    },
    "lagos-story": {
      "name": "Lagos: climate and health",
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 5,
        "extent": [
          -625615.5382581975,
          -276158.58202625543,
          1378135.2960207267,
          1749202.0876557613
        ],
        "transition": {
          "type": "smooth",
          "time": 1
        },
        "layerOverride": [],
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "## Lagos, Nigeria\n\nDiscuss mobility, host communities, food/water access and equity. Climate is not a deterministic cause of conflict. Movement counts are not distinct people and do not establish legal status.\n\n**Synthetic teaching scenario.** Not observations, forecasts or PEPFAR facility locations.\n\nExplore the [scenario dashboard](https://jltobias.github.io/JupyterLite-Climate-and-Health/explore/?case=lagos)."
        }
      }
    }
